   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_01.mp3",
     "text": "Hello, world. Some news is big. Some news is weird. Tonight, most of it is both. I'm Master K, and this is the Four Eyes Report."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_02.mp3",
     "screen": [
      "menu_shark",
      "menu_typhoon",
      "menu_psy",
      "menu_fridge"
     ],
     "big": true,
     "text": "Coming up: a shark that won't leave, a typhoon that never came, Psy, and a refrigerator you can date. Let's begin."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_03.mp3",
     "text": "Our top story: a shark. In a canal. In the middle of a city."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_04.mp3",
     "screen": "canal",
     "text": "Ten days ago, a three-and-a-half-meter shark swam into a narrow canal at Busan's North Port. And then it just... stayed."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_05.mp3",
     "screen": "requiem",
     "text": "Officials tried to guide it back to the sea. The shark declined."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_06.mp3",
     "text": "It DECLINED? Core, a shark cannot decline things."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_07.mp3",
     "text": "It's K. And technically, it can. It simply did not leave."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_08.mp3",
     "text": "What kind of shark is it, anyway?"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_09.mp3",
     "screen": "dusky",
     "text": "Probably a dusky shark. Or a copper shark. It declined to comment."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_10.mp3",
     "screen": "staycation",
     "big": true,
     "text": "So Korea did what Korea does. It gave the shark a nickname: Bukang-i. That's 'North Port', plus a cute little 'ee' on the end."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_11.mp3",
     "text": "Wait. WAIT. It has a nickname? Does it have a FANDOM?"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_12.mp3",
     "screen": "visitors",
     "big": true,
     "text": "Let's look at the numbers. Five hundred sixty-eight thousand, eight hundred visitors. Over the Chuseok holiday, one hundred forty thousand people came in a single day."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_13.mp3",
     "screen": "fifty",
     "big": true,
     "text": "On a normal holiday, this park gets about two thousand. That is a fiftyfold increase. For one shark."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_14.mp3",
     "text": "Half a million people in ten days? That's not a shark. That's a stadium tour."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_15.mp3",
     "screen": "farewell",
     "text": "The good news: scientists say Bukang-i is calm and healthy. Starting Tuesday morning, boats and water pumps will gently guide it back out to sea."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_16.mp3",
     "text": "So it's the farewell tour."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_bukang_17.mp3",
     "text": "K's Take: Only in Korea does a lost shark get a name, half a million fans, and a proper send-off. Bukang-i, safe travels."
    }
   ],
