   "lines": [
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_01.mp3",
     "text": "Okay. A shark that won't leave. What's next, weather that won't arrive?"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_02.mp3",
     "text": "...Did you read my script?"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_03.mp3",
     "text": "Next: the weather. Or rather, the weather that never showed up."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_04.mp3",
     "screen": [
      "tracks",
      "zero"
     ],
     "big": true,
     "screen_split": [
      0.55
     ],
     "text": "This year, not a single typhoon has made landfall in Korea. Not one."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_05.mp3",
     "text": "That's amazing! A free summer! Why do you look worried?"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_06.mp3",
     "text": "I always look like this. But yes, I'm worried."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_07.mp3",
     "screen": "bouncers",
     "big": true,
     "text": "For three summers now, two giant high-pressure systems, one from the Pacific and one from Tibet, have parked around Korea like bouncers outside a club."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_08.mp3",
     "screen": [
      "dolphin2",
      "dolphin1"
     ],
     "big": true,
     "text": "In August, Typhoon Dolphin crossed the Pacific, saw the line at the door, and headed toward Shanghai instead."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_09.mp3",
     "text": "Rejected at the door. Brutal."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_10.mp3",
     "screen": [
      "stormy",
      "calm"
     ],
     "text": "Here's the catch. Typhoons stir up the ocean. They mix cold, oxygen-rich water from below with the warm water on top. Scientists call them the ocean's ventilation system."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_11.mp3",
     "screen": "stuffy",
     "text": "So the ocean spent all summer in a stuffy room with the windows shut."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_12.mp3",
     "screen": [
      "seafarms",
      "fish",
      "drought"
     ],
     "big": true,
     "screen_split": [
      0.25,
      0.7
     ],
     "text": "Exactly. And fish farms are feeling it. Along the southern coast, about seven point seven million farmed fish have died this year. Rainfall is down about fifteen percent, and parts of the country are in drought."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_13.mp3",
     "text": "Okay. That's not a free summer at all."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_14.mp3",
     "screen": "hinnamnor",
     "text": "And experts warn: fewer typhoons can mean stronger ones later. Warm water is fuel."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_typhoon_15.mp3",
     "text": "K's Take: A quiet summer isn't always a good summer. Sometimes the calm is the story."
    }
   ],
