     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_01.mp3",
     "text": "Speaking of prior commitments..."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_02.mp3",
     "screen": "aircon",
     "text": "Finally tonight, a money story. In Korea, you can subscribe to... your air conditioner."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_03.mp3",
     "text": "Like Netflix? For an air conditioner?"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_04.mp3",
     "screen": "trillion",
     "big": true,
     "text": "Sort of. Samsung says its appliance subscription business is now approaching one trillion won in sales. That's about seven hundred forty million dollars."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_05.mp3",
     "screen": [
      "concept",
      "repair",
      "fridge"
     ],
     "text": "You pay monthly, and for the whole contract, engineers take care of maintenance, repairs and check-ups. It's less like streaming, and more like a very long rental."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_06.mp3",
     "screen": "date",
     "text": "So I don't own the fridge. The fridge and I are... in a relationship."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_07.mp3",
     "text": "A six-year relationship. With scheduled check-ins."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_08.mp3",
     "screen": "subs",
     "big": true,
     "text": "Let's look at the numbers. Ninety-four point eight percent of Koreans used a subscription service this year. The average person has five point five."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_09.mp3",
     "text": "Five point FIVE? Who has half a subscription?"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_10.mp3",
     "text": "Technically, it's an average. Nobody has half a subscription. ...Probably."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_11.mp3",
     "screen": [
      "hotel",
      "hospital",
      "moving"
     ],
     "text": "Now Samsung wants hotels, hospitals and public offices to subscribe too. There's even a plan for newlyweds and people who move a lot, with cleaning visits at night and on holidays."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_12.mp3",
     "text": "Night cleaning visits? That's not a subscription. That's a love language."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_13.mp3",
     "text": "K's Take: In Korea, even your washing machine comes with a care plan. We're still deciding whether that's the future, or just very, very organized."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_14.mp3",
     "text": "You can also subscribe to this channel. No six-year contract."
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_15.mp3",
     "shot": "wide",
     "text": "That's all for tonight. Stay curious. Keep your lenses clean."
    },
    {
     "who": "panel",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_16.mp3",
     "text": "So what are you doing this weekend?"
    },
    {
     "who": "anchor",
     "audio": "audio/ep01_samsung_17.mp3",
     "text": "Refreshing pages. Calmly."
    }
